  Also, the issue of bad performance due to absurdly large `history-limit` values is reported periodically. See, for example, [#3194](https://github.com/tmux/tmux/issues/3194) and [#2380](https://github.com/tmux/tmux/issues/2380). The latter issue pointing out that the memory required for humungous scrollback buffers is also likely to result in your system swapping processes in and out of memory. Which will also cause enormous slow downs.
  
  [@smemsh](https://github.com/smemsh): Why do you require such a huge scrollback history? Is there a legitimate use case or did you just stumble upon this problem because you didn't want to impose a realistic limit on the amount of scrollback history "just in case" more history was useful?
  
