  [@nicm](https://github.com/nicm): It might be a good idea to augment the documentation of the `history-limit` option to note the problems associated with large values. Such as increased physical and virtual memory consumption that can impact the performance of tmux and the system as a whole. I am not suggesting including details about PTEs and the like. Only that too many individuals seem to think unlimited scrollback history has no cost so it might help to note that it does, in fact, have a cost.
  
