  > I'm nowhere near the history limit
  
  You completely missed the points of my previous comments. You still haven't explained why you need such huge scrollback history. And you clearly do not understand the cost of an unreasonably large scrollback history.
  
  > I'm nowhere near the history limit and not describing a problem at those limits
  
  Which tells me you do not understand either my previous replies or how computers manage memory. Every single line in the tmux scrollback history requires memory. That physical, and virtual, memory also requires the operating system to use memory to manage that virtual memory.
  
  > Why are you governing my scrollback size and determining "legitimacy" on my behalf?
  
  Because capturing that history requires real, and virtual, storage. You seem to think that capturing an infinite scrollback history has zero cost.
  
  > Tmux is fast with the same scrollback sizes above, whenstatus-left is not set.
  
  Yes, as I explained in my previous comment that is due to the cost of the `fork()` syscall which is not relevant when you have not set a `status-left` definition that executes external programs.
  
