  You will need to take up issues with performance of `fork`/`exec` with kernel developers.
  
  I would accept a PR to make tmux use `posix_spawn` although of course you would need to figure out if it is supported on other platforms (Solaris and Cgywin would be the ones I would be most converned with) and provide a compatibility interface if not.
  
  Copy mode will be an issue with large histories because we now copy the history from the target pane. We used to use the history without copying, but for that we had to freeze writing to the pane to stop new output interfering with copying, and people hated that because it would cause long-running single-threaded processes to drop TCP connections. Possibly we could add some sort of copy-on-write and reference counting to `grid_line`, although of course that would increase memory consumption a little, and probably not be trivial to implement.
  
  Long term, I would like it if `history-limit` was shared across panes, so tmux would collect the oldest lines from rarely used panes to allow new ones to grow, and also if it was perhaps expressed in bytes or cells rather than lines. But that is a fair bit of work and nobody has done it yet.
  
  In the meantime you will need to avoid total history lines getting too big.
  
